Session summary 2026-10-01/02 (claude-interactive, /team /prd, session prd-df-864318). Authored and committed plans/write-triage-link-healing-prd.md, commit 8faca80c27 on branch task/6180. It is landing through merge carrier task 6180 (mr-6b386d45). It commits with it:
- fused-memory/calibration/hand_link_verdicts.jsonl, the 359 blind-rated hand links with majority rule and live text hashes;
- fused-memory/calibration/write_triage_rater_brief.md, byte-identical at the path λ 6152 names.

The design:
- one heal executor that corroborates before and verifies after each write, with an undo-capable ledger;
- two plan sources: the committed corpus and a rater-question adjudicator through the Claude CLI;
- a one-off cleanup of 237 actions (15 detaches, 80 sighting relabels, 64 amendment flags, 74 half-link completions, 4 dangling);
- add_memory kind guidance plus an inert-link ack;
- the adjudicator measured on the hand links behind gate Γ_A;
- the nightly sweep built after the flip (3169) behind a 'flip live' gate φ, a week in report mode, then a gate θ.

Seats: 4 sonnet evidence seats, an opus critic (24 findings, all integrated) and a sonnet corpus exporter.

Discoveries:
- The rater question has never been run as a detector by a non-rater model. The judge's distinct-veto has precision 0.13–0.44 on every arm.
- The ι scorer is judge-shaped, so detector metrics are computed directly.
- A cancelled dependency satisfies dependents, so each gate carries a delivered_check of kind script.

Decompose is handed off to a sibling session (brief: ~/.claude/spawn-briefs/link-healing-decompose-2026-10-02.md). Its commit_planning waits for the PRD to be on main.

