GOTCHA: pyright reports reportMissingImports on repo-root `scripts/` and `legibility` imports, and on cross-workspace-member imports, even when the venv and interpreter are configured CORRECTLY. The cause is extraPaths COMPLETENESS and INVOCATION CONTEXT -- not venv misconfiguration (that is the separate, already-closed task 3036 cluster; do not conflate them).

FOUR DISTINCT TRIGGERS, each documented by a stamped peer under topic `pyright-extrapaths-completeness`:
  - pyright `include` scoping leaving a path outside the analysed set;
  - a missing `--directory` invocation flag, so pyright resolves relative to the wrong root;
  - a sys.path.insert at runtime that extraPaths does not mirror, so it type-checks differently from how it runs;
  - a specific omission from the extraPaths list itself.

DIAGNOSE BY TRIGGER, not by symptom: all four surface as the same reportMissingImports line, so the symptom does not identify which one you have. Related but distinct: tests under tests/scripts/ importing from the flat scripts/ directory need `# pyright: ignore[reportMissingImports]` because repo-root scripts/ is deliberately absent from extraPaths -- that is topic `tests-scripts-pyright-ignore-extrapaths-absence` (gate 3509).

STANDING CAVEAT: task 3367's structural venvPath/venv fix may obsolete some documented workarounds. Re-verify against main before applying one.

ACCRETION: append to this entry or add a stamped peer under that topic -- do not write a new unstamped entry.

Fact, 2026-10-01: fused-memory/calibration/hand_link_verdicts.jsonl is the committed corpus of 359 blind-rated hand-made parent links. It landed with the link-healing PRD in b3b4415805. The 359 are the whole 2026-09-29 freeze (322 dark_factory + 41 reify) minus 4 links whose parents were already gone.

Row format:
- entry_id = child id, target_id = parent id;
- rater 'majority' with the majority word, plus a raters sub-dict {primary, second, third};
- the primary rater's reason;
- kind_at_rating, live child and parent sha256, rated_text_matches_live (true for all 359 at export).

Majority rule, ported from data/write-triage-stronger-models-2026-09-30/score_models.py::truth_l2:
- if the first two raters agree on both binaries (CORRECTS-vs-not, misfile-vs-not), the PRIMARY rater's word is kept, even when the second used a different belongs-word;
- otherwise the plurality of the three words wins;
- if all three differ, fixed tie-breaks apply.

Majority counts: EXTENDS 199, CORRECTS 111, SUBSUMED 32, RELATED 15, SAME 2, UNRELATED 0, UNCLEAR 0.

Text capping:
- Rating-time texts were capped at 4,000 chars with the suffix '…[truncated, N chars total]'.
- The 140 Γ2 'P' rows used a variant with a space before the ellipsis. That variant is INFERRED from 17 capped strings; no source script exists.

The rater brief is committed byte-identical at fused-memory/calibration/write_triage_rater_brief.md (sha256 7f161b0e…), the path λ (6152) names.

